  "notes": "{除菌|じょきん} combines {除|じょ} (remove) + {菌|きん} (bacteria), meaning to remove or reduce bacteria/germs.\n\nCommon expressions:\n- {除菌|じょきん}する (to sanitize)\n- {除菌|じょきん}シート (sanitizing wipes)\n- {除菌|じょきん}スプレー (sanitizing spray)\n- {除菌|じょきん}{効果|こうか} (sanitizing effect)\n- {除菌|じょきん}{力|りょく} (sanitizing power)\n\nRelated terms:\n- {殺菌|さっきん} (sterilization - killing bacteria)\n- {消毒|しょうどく} (disinfection - broader term)\n- {抗菌|こうきん} (antibacterial)\n\n{除菌|じょきん} became especially common during the COVID-19 pandemic.",
